{
  "id": 148464814,
  "iid": 6590,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "PROFINET: Fix count of IO data objects and IOCS",
  "description": "The number of IO data objects and IOCS is sometimes not calculated correctly, leading to errors like \"Too many data objects: xxx\". This may typically happen if the capture contains multiple Connect Requests where the ARUUID is the same.\n\nThis MR splits the counts of IO data objects and IOCS between input and output CRs. It also avoid incrementing these numbers while still taking into account multiple APIs in the IOCRBlock structures.\n\nCloses #18031 .",
